5,\"questions\":[{\"text\":\"In 2001, a 4.4-billion-year-old crystal from WA's Jack Hills was reported as the oldest known piece of Earth. What mineral is it?\",\"options\":[\"Garnet\",\"Zircon\",\"Olivine\",\"Quartz\"],\"answer\":\"Zircon\",\"marks\":[{\"team\":\"Quizzly Bears\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Les Quizerables\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Opera House Party\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false}]},{\"text\":\"A mosquito-borne virus isolated in 1974 is named after a forest in which state?\",\"options\":[\"Victoria\",\"Tasmania\",\"Western Australia\",\"Queensland\"],\"answer\":\"Victoria\",\"marks\":[{\"team\":\"Quizzly Bears\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Les Quizerables\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Opera House Party\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false}]},{\"text\":\"In 2024, Katherine Bennell-Pegg became the first astronaut trained under the Australian flag after completing training with which agency?\",\"answer\":\"European Space Agency\",\"marks\":[{\"team\":\"Quizzly Bears\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"Les Quizerables\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"Opera House Party\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false}]},{\"text\":\"Australia hosted a famous 1986 rendezvous for Halley-watchers, but in 1981 the nation's first cochlear implant recipient, Rod Saunders, received his device in which city?\",\"options\":[\"Sydney\",\"Brisbane\",\"Melbourne\",\"Adelaide\"],\"answer\":\"Melbourne\",\"marks\":[{\"team\":\"Quizzly Bears\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Les Quizerables\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false},{\"team\":\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":true},{\"team\":\"Opera House Party\",\"answer\":\"\",\"correct\":false}]}]}],\"notes\":\"# Venue notes\\n\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au` (or global).\\n- Format used in week 1: 6 rounds of 4 questions, as the trivia master asked. That was a one-off request for tonight, not a standing rule. The default is still 5 rounds of 8.\\n- Genres: the trivia master says the crowd loves film, and film went well (about 65% at difficulty 3, 75-90% at difficulty 2). Music and science were hard for them at difficulty 3 (about 45% and 35%). Sport was fine at difficulty 2 (about 65%).\\n- Week 1 gave no history or geography rounds, so give those a turn next week.\\n- Difficulty: start next night at 2. Difficulty 3 was too hard overall (about 48% correct) and difficulty 2 was a bit easy (about 77%). Step up one level only if a round goes over 75%.\\n- Week 1 ran with no answer sheets: the bank recorded answers as each round was served, and I checked round_summary instead of calling submit_round. Check how the trivia master wants it run next time.\\n\",\"steps\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01A5BptbUJKhYLM4pwgi3hSb\",\"name\":\"read\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"memories/MEMORY.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":100},\"result\":\"ENOENT: no such file or directory, access '/workspace/memories/MEMORY.md'\",\"error\":true},{\"id\":\"toolu_01UZTM37wqoWyKgUBqE3uJcz\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_start_night_33be65a290\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1}\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_013jbSatjmyoPz4wzkY5ZrRE\",\"name\":\"mcp_trivia-bank_register_teams_a86d67f229\",\"arguments\":{\"names\":[\"Quizzly Bears\",\"Les Quizerables\",\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"Opera House Party\"]},\"result\":\"{\\\"week\\\":1,\\\"teams\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Quizz