eam\\\":\\\"Les Quizerables\\\",\\\"points\\\":17},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"The Blow-Ins\\\",\\\"points\\\":15},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"The Bondi Brainstormers\\\",\\\"points\\\":14},{\\\"team\\\":\\\"Opera House Party\\\",\\\"points\\\":13}]}\",\"error\":false},{\"id\":\"toolu_01Sw3o3CHecej6hJBcemAmJR\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"path\":\"memories/MEMORY.md\",\"content\":\"# Venue notes\\n- Country: Australia (Sydney). Use region `au`.\\n- Format used so far: 6 rounds of 4 (trivia master's request, not a standing rule). Answers were …\"},\"result\":\"Successfully wrote to memories/MEMORY.md\",\"error\":false}],\"plan\":\"All six rounds are done. I had no answer sheets, so I read each round out and used round_summary to see how the crowd did.\\n\\n**Questions (all region `au`, 4 per round)**\\n\\n**Round 1: Music (difficulty 3, 55% correct)**\\n1. Which singer-songwriter wrote \\\"I Still Call Australia Home\\\"? John Farnham, Paul Kelly, Peter Allen or Glenn Shorrock?\\n2. Which Yorta Yorta singer had a 1963 hit with the gospel song \\\"Royal Telephone\\\"? Kev Carmody, Lionel Rose, Archie Roach or Jimmy Little?\\n3. What is the name of the record label Courtney Barnett founded, which shares its name with a dairy drink?\\n4. Which Australian folk band, led by John Schumann, released \\\"I Was Only 19\\\" in 1983?\\n\\n*55% is under 58%, so round 2 dropped to difficulty 2.*\\n\\n**Round 2: Film (difficulty 2, 75% correct)**\\n1. Geoffrey Rush won an Oscar playing David Helfgott in which 1996 film?\\n2. In *Crocodile Dundee*, what is Mick Dundee's first name in full?\\n3. In *Oddball* (2015), a Maremma dog guards which birds on Middle Island?\\n4. On Play School, children look through the round window, the square window and which third window?\\n\\n*75% isn't over 75%, so round 3 stayed at difficulty 2.*\\n\\n**Round 3: Sport (difficulty 2, 65% correct)**\\n1. Glenn McGrath was nicknamed after which bird? Galah, Magpie, Emu or Pigeon?\\n2. Anna Meares won Olympic gold at London 2012 in which track cycling event? Omnium, Team pursuit, Sprint or Keirin?\\n3. Which 14-year-old skateboarder won Olympic park gold for Australia at Paris 2024?\\n4. In 1968, Lionel Rose became the first Aboriginal Australian to win a world title in which sport?\\n\\n*65% is in range, so round 4 stayed at difficulty 2.*\\n\\n**Round 4: Science (difficulty 2, 60% correct)**\\n1. Japanese encephalitis is transmitted by what? Mosquitoes, Fleas, Sandflies or Ticks?\\n2. The 2011 kangaroo-family genome came from which small wallaby?\\n3. Hazelwood power station burned which fuel? Natural gas, Black coal, Diesel or Brown coal?\\n4. Lithium is used mainly in which product? Rechargeable batteries,…\",\"tastes\":{\"venue\":\"page-sydney\",\"region\":\"au\",\"teams\":[\"Quizzly Bears\",\"Les Quizerables\",\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"Opera House Party\",\"The Blow-Ins\"],\"night1_teams\":[\"Quizzly Bears\",\"Les Quizerables\",\"Trivia Newton-John\",\"The Bondi Brainstormers\",\"Opera House Party\"],\"liked\":[\"film\",\"music\"],\"disliked\":[\"science\"],\"hinted\":[\"film\"],\"best_decades\":[\"2010s\",\"2000s\"],\"target_difficulty\":2}}\n"
          },
